nants' active reservations sum to the two limits, never collapse into one bucket). The cross-tenant sum-check is the load-bearing defence-in-depth: per-tenant counts could pass while a regression silently dropped one tenant's rows entirely. The SECURITY.md substring set MUST include `FOR UPDATE` (the lock) and `organization_id` (the predicate) so an auditor verifies the invariant from the documented contract alone, without opening the test file. Forward-applicable to ANY future concurrency-verification story whose invariant has a "single-tenant hot path × cross-tenant isolation path" dual: BE-0386 (fake Dokploy), BE-0398 (tenant isolation), BE-0407 (service desired-state goldens). (3) `VERIFY.SH RENUMBER OF OPTIONALS BLOCK CONTINUES` — inserting required step #10 between #9 (policy matrix) and the optionals renumbered 10→11/11→12/12→13/13→14 in the same edit (govulncheck/staticcheck/golangci-lint/goreleaser). The static test pins `# 10. Required: quota concurrency tests` but NOT the optional headers — those shift on every required insertion. Established by BE-0380's renumber pattern. Per-story knobs for siblings: (a) canonical command (BE-0384 uses `go test -run TestQuotaConcurrency ./...` filter-narrowed; BE-0385 will use `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...`), (b) dedicated CI step name (BE-0384: "Quota concurrency tests"), (c) verify.sh numeric prefix (next number after the last required step; renumber trailing optionals in the same edit), (d) SECURITY.md section heading and 13-entry substring set covering scope / determinism / actionable-failures (engine-specific tokens: FOR UPDATE, organization_id, CodeQuotaExceeded) / opt-in-external / envelope-pinning / canonical-pair / redaction / CI-cadence / self-locating gate filename, (e) PRD requiredBackendCommands entry pre-existing OR newly inserted, (f) canonical reference test file path + canonical-pair func-name set + the `-run` filter prefix the canonical-funcs entries MUST satisfy. Load-bearing invariant: ONE FILE, SIX SURFACES, SELF-CHECK; drift on any surface fails ONE test, not six. GOTCHA: in TestQuotaConcurrencyTenantIsolation's per-org goroutine closure, do NOT alias `t` (the *testing.T) to a per-tenant tally bucket — `t := results[orgID]` SHADOWS the outer testing.T, silently breaking `t.Errorf` inside the closure. Used `bucket := results[orgID]` to keep the testing.T accessible for actionable diagnostics. Forward-applicable to any verification-suite story whose parallel-goroutine test groups results per-loop-var.
