ralph/prd.json:9007:      "notes": "Repository-layer tenant-isolation coverage for the organizations source-of-truth landed as internal/controlplane/store/organization_tenant_isolation_test.go. Seven new integration tests prove (1) Get is keyed strictly by the row's own id and returns each tenant's own row, never another's; (2) an unknown organization_id is the same typed NotFound a principal sees for another tenant's id; (3) Update on orgA leaves orgB byte-identical (slug, display_name, version, updated_at, deletion_scheduled_at); (4) a stale-If-Match Update on orgA also leaves orgB byte-identical; (5) ScheduleDeletion on orgA stamps only orgA and never bleeds the stamp into orgB; (6) a soft-deleted orgA is still readable as its own row without masking orgB visibility; (7) slug uniqueness is globally enforced across the tenant root with a typed Conflict and the failed Insert lands no row. Tests run under -race against an isolated, freshly migrated Postgres database via YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL and skip when unset. gofmt -w, go mod tidy, go vet ./..., go test ./..., and go test -race -count=1 -run TestOrganizationRepository ./internal/controlplane/store/... all pass. The organizations table has no list-by-parent method at the repository layer (it is the tenant root); /v1/me/organizations is a membership-derived join handled at the httpapi layer and its tenant-isolation property is covered by the membership repository tests. goimports/golangci-lint/staticcheck/govulncheck are not installed locally."
ralph/prd.json:9045:      "notes": "Repository-layer tenant-isolation coverage for the users global identity table landed as internal/controlplane/store/user_tenant_isolation_test.go. Six new integration tests prove (1) Get by id returns each tenant's own row across two seeded organizations and never merges or swaps rows; (2) Update on userA leaves userB byte-identical including the trigger-driven updated_at; (3) an Update on userA that tries to claim userB's email under a different casing fails typed Conflict via the citext UNIQUE constraint and leaves BOTH users byte-identical (no partial-write damage on the target row, no trigger-refreshed timestamp on the bystander); (4) Delete on userA removes userA, cascades userA's memberships across every tenant via memberships(user_id) ON DELETE CASCADE, and leaves userB and userB's memberships byte-identical; (5) Insert of an intruder row whose email is an upper-cased copy of an existing email under a peer tenant fails typed Conflict, the intruder row never lands, and the original userA row is byte-identical including updated_at; (6) GetInOrganization with an unknown user id and GetInOrganization with a real-but-non-member user id produce the same yerr.CodeNotFound shape with matching Hint values, so existence cannot be inferred from the response code or hint. Files: internal/controlplane/store/user_tenant_isolation_test.go (new). The list-by-parent and soft-delete acceptance criteria are intentionally documented as not-applicable in the file's package-doc comment: users has no parent (the per-tenant roster lives on memberships, proven by membership_test.go) and no deletion_scheduled_at column (human identities are hard-deleted with cascade)."
ralph/prd.json:9216:      "notes": "Added internal/controlplane/store/project_repository_invariants_test.go with eight new t.Parallel tests covering the row-shape and lifecycle invariants the existing project_test.go / project_delete_test.go / project_restore_test.go did not anchor: Insert returns version=1 with byte-equal created_at == updated_at and nil deletion_scheduled_at; Update / UpdateDisplayName / ScheduleDeletion / Restore each prove the full dual-anchor (version+1, updated_at refreshed, created_at preserved) plus their path-specific column invariants (UpdateDisplayName preserves slug; ScheduleDeletion stamps deletion_scheduled_at on/after the update boundary; Restore clears it back to NULL; identity fields preserved on both); a matching-If-Match Update anchors the positive optimistic-concurrency path; Insert participates in the surrounding tx as the unit of work (rolls back across Get / List / Count); and a typed nil-Tx guard on UpdateDisplayName closes the only Project mutation path that did not yet have a typed-code assertion. All eight pass against an isolated, freshly migrated Postgres. gofmt / go vet / go test ./... / go test -race ./internal/controlplane/store/ all clean. Pre-existing flaky tests in apikeyservice / environmentservice / variable services are unrelated and documented in prior progress."
ralph/prd.json:9368:      "notes": "Added internal/controlplane/store/service_repository_invariants_test.go (9 tests + 2 file-scope helpers + 1 typed rollback sentinel) covering ServiceRepository CRUD row-shape and lifecycle invariants for Insert, Update, ScheduleDeletion, and Restore. Tests prove: Insert returns row at version=1 with byte-equal created_at/updated_at and nil deletion_scheduled_at; Update bumps version by exactly +1, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at AND the composite (organization_id, project_id, environment_id) tenant key AND the immutable Dokploy taxonomy 'kind' (Update's SET clause must touch slug/display_name only); Update with matching If-Match succeeds; ScheduleDeletion bumps version, refreshes updated_at, preserves identity (slug/display_name/kind) and tenant key, and stamps deletion_scheduled_at at or after baseline.UpdatedAt; Restore is the inverse — bumps version, refreshes updated_at, preserves identity and tenant key, and clears deletion_scheduled_at back to NULL; Insert participates in the surrounding transaction (closure error rolls back the row, invisible at GetByID and ListByEnvironment); Insert/Update/ScheduleDeletion nil-Tx guards render typed apierr.Internal (Restore's nil-Tx guard already covered by TestServiceRepositoryRestoreRejectsNilTx in service_restore_test.go). gofmt, go vet, go build, go mod tidy, go test ./..., and go test -race ./... all green; new tests skip when YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL is unset (local Postgres container has no published port, matching BE-0001/BE-0443/BE-0444 contract)."
