diff --git a/ralph/progress.txt b/ralph/progress.txt
index 8f219b508df4363626d6e056a8185c7959371be7..376f92ff415e5cb427da744690763516c9145851
--- a/ralph/progress.txt
+++ b/ralph/progress.txt
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 - Audit event metrics follow the existing low-cardinality telemetry collector pattern: `telemetry.AuditEventMetrics` groups by `(action, resource_kind, decision, outcome, reason, error_code)`, stores request/correlation/org/resource/actor/job IDs only as latest-sample incident hints, is emitted from `store.AuditRepository.Append` for both recorded and failed append attempts, and `/metrics` exposes the snapshot under `data.audit_events`.
 - Backoffice runtime config consumers should use `backoffice.RuntimeConfigCache` over `AdminConfigRepository.ListActivePublishedRuntime`: snapshots are immutable, carry `config_set_id`/`version_id`/`version`/`revision` identifiers, continue serving the last known good config after reload failures, and emit one stale alert per generation once the configured staleness threshold is exceeded.
 - Backoffice attribution rules are dedicated global runtime metering contracts: `admin_attribution_rules` stores enabled rules ordered by `(priority, rule_key)`, mutations go through `AdminAttributionRuleService` for actor-org verification plus audit in one `Store.Write`, and dry-run evaluation is side-effect free with unsafe samples rendered as attributed/quarantined/ignored but never billable unless a rule meets its configured confidence threshold.
+- Backoffice usage aggregation schedules are dedicated global runtime metering contracts: `admin_usage_aggregation_schedules` stores one schedule per `(source, metric_key)`, updates in place with monotonically increasing `version`/`revision`, disables instead of deleting, exposes enabled runtime reload through `UsageAggregationScheduleRepository.ListRuntimeEnabled`, and mutates through `AdminUsageAggregationScheduleService` so actor-org verification plus audit happen in one `Store.Write`.
 - Backoffice metric definitions use dedicated versioned global config, not generic JSON config: `admin_metric_definitions` keeps one current row per key (`superseded_at IS NULL`), `MetricDefinitionRepository.Upsert` rejects billing-grade unit changes unless `AllowNewVersion` is set and then inserts the next version, runtime aggregators reload enabled current rows through `ListRuntimePublished`, and HTTP routes are support-gated with `admin.metering.manage`.
 - Backoffice metering source configuration uses a dedicated audited store surface rather than generic JSON config when credentials are involved: persist global `admin_metering_sources` rows with write-only `(credential_provider, credential_key_id, credential_ciphertext)` columns, return only `credential_set` on the wire, expose runtime reload through `MeteringSourceRepository.ListRuntimeEnabled`, and gate HTTP routes with `admin.metering.manage` (currently CapSupport).
 - Quota usage metrics follow the existing HTTP/job/Dokploy collector pattern: one in-memory `telemetry.QuotaUsageMetrics` series per low-cardinality `(resource, enforcement_mode, outcome, reason)` tuple, with request/correlation/org/principal/job IDs and quota counts kept only as latest-sample incident hints. The quota checker emits decisions for allowed, rejected, validation, and infrastructure-error paths, and `/metrics` exposes the snapshot under `data.quota_usage`.
@@ -38760,3 +38761,55 @@
